{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079609-help-on-a-abyssal-cult-idea","id":1079609,"title":"Help on a Abyssal cult idea.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-16T18:43:26-07:00","id":1079609,"title":"Help on a Abyssal cult idea.","content":"I thought up a cult to use in a mage chronicle. They are a agricultural firm named Demeter Inc. They look for ways to artificially grow crops and other agricultural products. But, they have a secret they wish to keep buried. They serve the Abyss and it's eldritch inhabitants. They are led by a scalesti by the name of Alfred Oglethrop,a Englishman who wants to use the company to spread abyssal taint through it's produce.<br /> <br /> I need help detailing how they spread taint through crops and detailing their Mystery Cult merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:25:00-07:00","id":1079632,"title":"","content":"I mean, the obvious thing with spreading taint through crops is &quot;if you eat the crops, you're infected&quot;. Maybe eating the crops slowly mutates you into an abyssal monster, or opens you up to possession. More subtly, perhaps it increases the amount of &quot;abyssal energy&quot; in the person, making them count more towards helping paradoxes (Or more vulnerable to paradoxes if they're mages). This leads to an increase in abyssal activity in the area but it would require you spending some effort to figure out it's the new cheap food behind it.<br /> <br /> Alternately, it could be the plants themselves that links to the abyss. Maybe they naturally grow in glyphs, and every new moon another terrible thing crawls out of the cornyards. Or maybe they corrupt the ecosystem, replacing earthly animals and plants with abyssal versions. It can start out subtle near the edges, just weirdly-mutated plants and animals, and as you get closer to the centre of the artificial habitat it turns into an abyssal nightmare jungle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T21:02:59-07:00","id":1079671,"title":"","content":"What anti-truth are they trying to spread?<br /> Is it a flesh eating plant, miracle wheat that will grow anywhere, what?<br /> Perhaps it is addictive to all those who eat it and enticing to everyone, even carnivore animals.<br /> Don't limit yourself to its effect on those who eat their products either, its biggest effect might be on the environment where it grows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T04:05:03-07:00","id":1079738,"title":"","content":"*considers* The wheat is sentient! By eating the wheat, you slowly become smarter, stronger, faster etc - not because of any nutritional value but because of the sentience that lays inside all living things. Taking this antitruth is easy to take one step further when you realize how many other things are sentient as well - perhaps you could gather power from other sources?<br /> <br /> No seriously though it would be easier to help if you defined what the Abyssal Cult believed and what they follow. I have one cult for instance which follows an entity known as the Silence, and they are big on the idea that there is too much noise, so no one can hear anything that is being said - by god, by the people around them, etc - and if the world was engulfed in pure Silence then there would be a world where everyone truly understood one another.<br /> <br /> Having an idea of what kind of direction this Abyssal cult was going would definitely help determine what benefits the cult gave <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T04:46:44-07:00","id":1079744,"title":"","content":"Another thing to remember is that the Abyss is the home of the &quot;impossible&quot;, not merely corruption and decay and evil. They could be leveraging some beneficial Abyssal property like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6084\" data-vbnamecard=\"6084\">2ptTakrill</a>'s grow-anywhere wheat, some heals-anything lettuce, or makes-you-stronger fruit, etc. Just as long as what it does <i>does not work that way</i>. The side-effects, of course, are completely unintentional, and will certainly be eliminated given enough time and research into the effects... as they assure you.<br /> <hr /><br /> Demeter Inc, eh? What about plants that can grow in impossibly nutrient poor soil, low temperatures, and with little to no light - ideal for winter conditions. Because that is where they come from, an Abyssal reality where the world is covered in eternal winter. The only problem is enough concentrations of these plants (and their material - it persists for some time, even after being digested) brings that &quot;reality&quot; closer - temperatures start to fall, light grows fainter, etc.<br /> <br /> Hey, maybe the side-effect are a fringe benefit, Demeter Inc reasons - combat hunger <i>and</i> global warming in one go!<br /> <br /> If only it didn't frequently spawn the Abyssal version of Ghosts (as opposed to Acamoth and Gulmoth) so often...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-17-2017, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:18:22-07:00","id":1079890,"title":"","content":"You could do some sort of Abyssal Roses of Eden?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13276-bristark","name":"Bristark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13276_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:18:36-07:00","id":1079891,"title":"","content":"So, here's an interesting feature of plants: Totipotency. Every plant cell, bar a few specialized, non-nucleated ones, can dedifferentiate into a totipotent stem cell in response to environmental signaling. This is why you can, say, take a cutting of a plant and grow a new one from it.<br /> <br /> What if their goal really is benevolent and they want to use plants for good? Wheat that can grow on concrete, or completely without water. You can grind it up into flour and eat it with no ill effects.<br /> <br /> And it's true. You can.<br /> <br /> Until someone on a health kick decides they want whole grain. <br /> <br /> Then, suddenly, you have people dying in agony as their flesh becomes fertilizer for the plant. Worse, turns out that this isn't something the plants will pass up. Suddenly you have vegetable zombies stalking the land, force-feeding people lettuce.<br /> <br /> And out in the fields, there the corpses gather to bow in worship of He Who Walks Between the Rows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:58:42-07:00","id":1080026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079609-help-on-a-abyssal-cult-idea?p=1079744#post1079744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing to remember is that the Abyss is the home of the &quot;impossible&quot;, not merely corruption and decay and evil. They could be leveraging some beneficial Abyssal property like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6084\" data-vbnamecard=\"6084\">2ptTakrill</a>'s grow-anywhere wheat, some heals-anything lettuce, or makes-you-stronger fruit, etc. Just as long as what it does <i>does not work that way</i>. The side-effects, of course, are completely unintentional, and will certainly be eliminated given enough time and research into the effects... as they assure you.<br /> <hr /><br /> Demeter Inc, eh? What about plants that can grow in impossibly nutrient poor soil, low temperatures, and with little to no light - ideal for winter conditions. Because that is where they come from, an Abyssal reality where the world is covered in eternal winter. The only problem is enough concentrations of these plants (and their material - it persists for some time, even after being digested) brings that &quot;reality&quot; closer - temperatures start to fall, light grows fainter, etc.<br /> <br /> Hey, maybe the side-effect are a fringe benefit, Demeter Inc reasons - combat hunger <i>and</i> global warming in one go!<br /> <br /> If only it didn't frequently spawn the Abyssal version of Ghosts (as opposed to Acamoth and Gulmoth) so often...</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the idea of the plants causing a eternal winter. Perhaps the corps goal is to stop global warming by making the planet cooler. But, the scalesti in charge wants to bring his abyssal master into the world by making the world colder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T18:16:48-07:00","id":1080114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079609-help-on-a-abyssal-cult-idea?p=1080026#post1080026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the idea of the plants causing a eternal winter. Perhaps the corps goal is to stop global warming by making the planet cooler. But, the scalesti in charge wants to bring his abyssal master into the world by making the world colder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works.<br /> <br /> Though, do they <i>need</i> to have a &quot;mwuahahah&quot; motivation? Wouldn't solving world hunger and global warming be enough? They are just blind to the long term consequences. Some sympathetic greyness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-17-2017, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T18:39:57-07:00","id":1080125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079609-help-on-a-abyssal-cult-idea?p=1080114#post1080114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Works.<br /> <br /> Though, do they <i>need</i> to have a &amp;quot;mwuahahah&amp;quot; motivation? Wouldn't solving world hunger and global warming be enough? They are just blind to the long term consequences. Some sympathetic greyness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, them being unaware of the consequence could be better. Well, their boss probably knows what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T23:02:47-07:00","id":1080195,"title":"","content":"Jim Jones didn't get people to sign on by saying &quot;Hey, let's all move to Cuba and drink punch!&quot;<br /> \u200bInstead he went around to people who had been disillusioned on changing the world and said &quot;We can build a community without greed or need, without rich or poor.&quot; and they thought that sounded like a good idea, a community like that might be feasible, so they joined in. It was only later after they had gotten in too deep, were too invested in him (or staring down a gun) that people found out about the punch.<br /> \u200bGroups like this first form by offering people something beneficial, even if it's just a target for their hate, then only later do the Nazis tell them about the death camps, after they've been lead down the primrose path far enough to accept it and mistake it for good.<br /> It's even possible their boss doesn't know the full truth of what's ahead, just enough that he still thinks the end justifies the means.<br /> \u200bTo quote Dr. Strange: &quot;They put the warnings after the spells.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}